    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section reports a confirmatory factor analysis conducted in the second split-half subsample (n=475), testing a one-factor model of BAS-2 scores with initial poor fit (e.g., robust RMSEA = .103). After freeing specified error covariances (Items 6&7, 1&6, 3&4) model fit improved (robust RMSEA = .080), with omega = .88 and AVE = .57 indicating acceptable reliability and convergent validity.",
      "evidence_source": "In the second split-half subsample (n=475), we examined the fit of a one-factor model of BAS-2 scores. These modifications resulted in an adequately fitting model, SB\u03c72(32) = 111.454, SB\u03c72_{normed} = 3.48, robust RMSEA = .080 (90% CI=.068\u2013.103), SRMR=.043, robust CFI=.950, robust TLI=.930, BL89=.945. In this subsample, omega was .88 (95% CI=.85\u2013.91). The convergent validity for this model was adequate, as AVE was greater than .50 (AVE=.57).",
